WEBVTT

1
01:10:12.194 --> 01:10:16.194
Hallelujah. Everyone happy? Glad.

2
01:10:20.194 --> 01:10:30.194
I find it very nice in the last few months that we have been doing a Bible study together as a church.

3
01:10:30.194 --> 01:10:36.194
I don't know what you think about it, but I personally find it just very nice. Thank you.

4
01:10:36.194 --> 01:10:42.194
The reason I enjoy going through the Bible as a church,

5
01:10:42.194 --> 01:10:48.194
is because when you take a book of the Bible, I have mentioned this several times in the last few weeks,

6
01:10:48.194 --> 01:10:58.194
but when you preach on what you want to choose at that moment, you will pick themes,

7
01:10:58.194 --> 01:11:02.194
and with those themes, you will say, oh, I like to preach on this, and I like to preach on that.

8
01:11:02.194 --> 01:11:06.194
And there is actually nothing wrong with that, only there is a risk involved,

9
01:11:06.194 --> 01:11:10.194
because the risk is that you might skip important themes.

10
01:11:10.194 --> 01:11:16.194
Because sometimes important themes are not the most enjoyable themes to teach.

11
01:11:16.194 --> 01:11:22.194
By the way, it is not a proclamation that it will be a difficult theme later, that is not what I am going to say.

12
01:11:22.194 --> 01:11:29.194
But what I like about going through the Bible, what I find healthy about it,

13
01:11:29.194 --> 01:11:35.194
is that you go through the Bible and you encounter step by step what the Bible teaches.

14
01:11:35.194 --> 01:11:39.194
And you go through it together, and then you study it together.

15
01:11:39.194 --> 01:11:47.194
And then as a church, you have a sort of checklist that you have explored God's Word together,

16
01:11:47.194 --> 01:11:49.194
that you all learn from it.

17
01:11:49.194 --> 01:11:53.194
And so with this Chronicles Bible study that we are doing,

18
01:11:53.194 --> 01:11:59.194
I had quickly brought up at the beginning of the service, okay, what have we actually done.

19
01:11:59.194 --> 01:12:04.194
In Chronicles, for example, we have addressed the theme of what the theme of Chronicles itself is.

20
01:12:04.194 --> 01:12:06.194
And that is a message of hope.

21
01:12:06.194 --> 01:12:09.194
For we have a hopeful God, can I get an amen on that?

22
01:12:09.194 --> 01:12:15.194
We have a God who, amidst the mess we often make of our own lives,

23
01:12:15.194 --> 01:12:17.194
we have a God of hope.

24
01:12:17.194 --> 01:12:21.194
And His name is Jesus. He stormed to a cross for my sin,

25
01:12:21.194 --> 01:12:27.194
so that I do not have to remain in my sin, but that I may rise from the dead in the righteousness of Jesus.

26
01:12:27.194 --> 01:12:31.194
So we have discussed the theme of hope.

27
01:12:31.194 --> 01:12:35.194
And then we talked about that list of names.

28
01:12:35.194 --> 01:12:37.194
Your name is a story.

29
01:12:37.194 --> 01:12:41.194
And I hope that your name is a story that relates to God.

30
01:12:41.194 --> 01:12:45.194
That when you ultimately come face to face with the Creator,

31
01:12:45.194 --> 01:12:47.194
He says, I like your story.

32
01:12:47.194 --> 01:12:52.194
It is history, it is His story, it is His whole story.

33
01:12:52.194 --> 01:12:57.194
But it is so cool if your name is written in the palm of God,

34
01:12:57.194 --> 01:12:59.194
in the book of life.

35
01:12:59.194 --> 01:13:02.194
And that ultimately when you see Him face to face,

36
01:13:02.194 --> 01:13:05.194
He says, come in my son, you have done well.

37
01:13:05.194 --> 01:13:07.194
Your name matters.

38
01:13:07.194 --> 01:13:11.194
Next, we talked about the disobedience and the sin of Saul,

39
01:13:11.194 --> 01:13:13.194
which ultimately led to his death.

40
01:13:13.194 --> 01:13:17.194
And it is important as a church that we teach about obedience.

41
01:13:17.194 --> 01:13:24.194
And so that is really another topic that has been under discussion since the 2000s.

42
01:13:24.194 --> 01:13:27.194
Obedience, it is much more enjoyable to talk about blessings.

43
01:13:27.194 --> 01:13:30.194
It is much more enjoyable to talk about being protected.

44
01:13:30.194 --> 01:13:34.194
It is much more enjoyable to talk about God being the provider.

45
01:13:34.194 --> 01:13:37.194
But then you come as a church to talk about obedience.

46
01:13:38.194 --> 01:13:44.194
But do you know how nice it is to know how important it is to be obedient to God,

47
01:13:44.194 --> 01:13:47.194
so that you can live in the blessing of God.

48
01:13:47.194 --> 01:13:49.194
For where is true freedom?

49
01:13:49.194 --> 01:13:54.194
Is it freedom to do what you want and reap the consequences?

50
01:13:54.194 --> 01:13:58.194
Or is it true freedom to live in the protection of God?

51
01:13:58.194 --> 01:14:03.194
That the Creator of heaven and earth says, I have made heaven and earth this way.

52
01:14:03.194 --> 01:14:06.194
I am the Creator, I know how it works.

53
01:14:06.194 --> 01:14:10.194
And I want you to behave this way, for that has been my intention for your life.

54
01:14:10.194 --> 01:14:12.194
And if you do that, then you will be blessed.

55
01:14:12.194 --> 01:14:14.194
There lies the freedom.

56
01:14:14.194 --> 01:14:16.194
I discovered that at the age of 24.

57
01:14:16.194 --> 01:14:21.194
That obedience to God actually gives freedom, actually gives peace.

58
01:14:21.194 --> 01:14:24.194
Obedience is not a difficult topic.

59
01:14:24.194 --> 01:14:27.194
It is just a topic that we do need to address.

60
01:14:27.194 --> 01:14:28.194
Do you understand what I mean?

61
01:14:28.194 --> 01:14:30.194
We have also talked about that dedication.

62
01:14:30.194 --> 01:14:33.194
And that dedication must be in the way of God.

63
01:14:33.194 --> 01:14:36.194
For Uzzah touched the cart, and Uzzah died.

64
01:14:36.194 --> 01:14:40.194
And Uzzah touched the cart because he wanted to do something good on one hand,

65
01:14:40.194 --> 01:14:43.194
but on the other hand, it was not God's intention in that way.

66
01:14:43.194 --> 01:14:49.194
And so it is good that we as a church learn that we must engage with God in the way that God wants.

67
01:14:49.194 --> 01:14:51.194
That we do not make our own God.

68
01:14:51.194 --> 01:14:52.194
Do you understand what I mean?

69
01:14:52.194 --> 01:14:58.194
Sometimes I talk to people, even in the church, who say yes, but God is this and God is that.

70
01:14:58.194 --> 01:15:03.194
And sometimes I talk in the church with people who hold various perspectives.

71
01:15:03.194 --> 01:15:07.194
That I think to myself, yes but where do you get that from? That does not come from the Bible.

72
01:15:07.194 --> 01:15:09.194
Yes, but God is this and I think God is that.

73
01:15:09.194 --> 01:15:13.194
Yes, but wait, wait. We must align it with the Bible.

74
01:15:13.194 --> 01:15:17.194
We must use God's Word, for God's Word is His Word.

75
01:15:17.194 --> 01:15:18.194
This is who God is.

76
01:15:18.194 --> 01:15:21.194
So in the Bible, you can find out who God is.

77
01:15:21.194 --> 01:15:25.194
Not in your own emotions, because that is of course wow.

78
01:15:25.194 --> 01:15:26.194
Do you understand what I mean?

79
01:15:26.194 --> 01:15:31.194
No opinion, but we have God's Word to know who the Lord is. Amen.

80
01:15:31.194 --> 01:15:33.194
We have talked about worship.

81
01:15:33.194 --> 01:15:37.194
That David began to talk about how worship works.

82
01:15:37.194 --> 01:15:39.194
What worship is and how you do it.

83
01:15:39.194 --> 01:15:46.194
And it's super cool to see that thousands of years later we still come together in the church to worship God.

84
01:15:46.194 --> 01:15:49.194
That is important. That is one of the most important tools.

85
01:15:50.194 --> 01:15:56.194
What struck me immensely, because as a pastor on a stage you learn about the most compared to everyone in the audience.

86
01:15:56.194 --> 01:15:59.194
Because you are busy with it all week and you shouldn't think that I know everything, everything, everything.

87
01:15:59.194 --> 01:16:01.194
And suppose I knew everything, everything, everything.

88
01:16:01.194 --> 01:16:05.194
As you read it, you learn and learn, while you are preaching it.

89
01:16:05.194 --> 01:16:08.194
It's just beautiful to keep going through God's Word.

90
01:16:08.194 --> 01:16:10.194
God's Word never stops.

91
01:16:10.194 --> 01:16:14.194
It is a source of living water and it just keeps going and going.

92
01:16:14.194 --> 01:16:16.194
It is so amazing.

93
01:16:16.194 --> 01:16:21.194
And then it is so cool to see that the heart of God lies in worship.

94
01:16:21.194 --> 01:16:23.194
God loves obedience.

95
01:16:23.194 --> 01:16:24.194
God loves giving.

96
01:16:24.194 --> 01:16:26.194
God loves working.

97
01:16:26.194 --> 01:16:29.194
But David could touch God's heart.

98
01:16:29.194 --> 01:16:35.194
Because David knew that he could touch God's heart with music and with worship.

99
01:16:35.194 --> 01:16:38.194
That is why David was a man after God's heart.

100
01:16:38.194 --> 01:16:39.194
Awesome.

101
01:16:39.194 --> 01:16:43.194
And last week we talked about righteousness.

102
01:16:43.194 --> 01:16:45.194
Another topic like that.

103
01:16:45.194 --> 01:16:47.194
Righteousness is important.

104
01:16:47.194 --> 01:16:51.194
David goes into battle against hostile nations and David prevails.

105
01:16:51.194 --> 01:16:58.194
And even in war, we see that when David fights on the natural earth,

106
01:16:58.194 --> 01:17:00.194
he is waging war against demonic powers.

107
01:17:00.194 --> 01:17:02.194
We can see it that way.

108
01:17:02.194 --> 01:17:04.194
And God is a just God.

109
01:17:04.194 --> 01:17:07.194
Who in this room believes that we have a just God?

110
01:17:07.194 --> 01:17:09.194
And all hands should go up.

111
01:17:09.194 --> 01:17:16.194
For we do not have a God who says, just look, I am gracious.

112
01:17:16.194 --> 01:17:18.194
So just do as you please.

113
01:17:18.194 --> 01:17:20.194
And I will overlook it.

114
01:17:20.194 --> 01:17:22.194
No, this is not the God we honor.

115
01:17:22.194 --> 01:17:24.194
We have a God of truth.

116
01:17:24.194 --> 01:17:27.194
God who says, this is the truth.

117
01:17:27.194 --> 01:17:29.194
And if you do not follow that truth, it is sin.

118
01:17:29.194 --> 01:17:33.194
And if you sin, you will simply receive the wages of sin.

119
01:17:33.194 --> 01:17:36.194
And that is death and death in hell without Jesus.

120
01:17:36.194 --> 01:17:40.194
Without God, without Christians, without His people.

121
01:17:40.194 --> 01:17:42.194
That is what awaits us.

122
01:17:42.194 --> 01:17:44.194
We do not have a God who says, just take a look.

123
01:17:44.194 --> 01:17:47.194
We have a God who says, I find it so important

124
01:17:47.194 --> 01:17:52.194
that we know what the truth is, that I have given my son.

125
01:17:52.194 --> 01:17:57.194
So that everyone who believes in Jesus shall not perish, but have eternal life.

126
01:17:57.194 --> 01:17:59.194
So we must build our hope on Jesus.

127
01:17:59.194 --> 01:18:01.194
For without Jesus, you won't make it, people.

128
01:18:01.194 --> 01:18:04.194
Praise the Lord, I am so happy.

129
01:18:32.194 --> 01:18:37.194
Very often when we talk about sins, we quickly bring up uncleanness.

130
01:18:37.194 --> 01:18:41.194
Very often when we talk about sins, we quickly bring up addictions.

131
01:18:41.194 --> 01:18:46.194
Very often when we talk about sins, we talk about aggressiveness and uncleanness

132
01:18:46.194 --> 01:18:49.194
and alcohol and I don't know what else.

133
01:18:49.194 --> 01:18:55.194
But pride is one of the important major sins in the Bible

134
01:18:55.194 --> 01:19:00.194
that we must expose and that we must cast out of our lives.

135
01:19:00.194 --> 01:19:03.194
And we don't have to make much effort ourselves,

136
01:19:03.194 --> 01:19:06.194
for someone has died on a cross.

137
01:19:06.194 --> 01:19:11.194
So that in the name of Jesus we can address this sin

138
01:19:11.194 --> 01:19:15.194
and cleanse it from our lives in Jesus' mighty name.

139
01:19:15.194 --> 01:19:19.194
Therefore the communion in the name of Jesus.

140
01:19:19.194 --> 01:19:24.194
If you have your Bible with you, turn with me to 1 Chronicles chapter 21.

141
01:19:24.194 --> 01:19:31.194
I will just read it to him in Flashlight Superspeed times 2.

142
01:19:31.194 --> 01:19:35.194
So that’s 27 verses.

143
01:19:35.194 --> 01:19:38.194
I think you can all join me in this, right?

144
01:19:38.194 --> 01:19:40.194
Tension arc!

145
01:19:44.194 --> 01:19:47.194
Are you all at 1 Chronicles chapter 21?

146
01:19:48.194 --> 01:19:50.194
Say amen if you are there.

147
01:19:50.194 --> 01:19:52.194
That’s good enough.

148
01:19:55.194 --> 01:19:58.194
Do you know what is difficult in sermon preparation?

149
01:19:58.194 --> 01:20:02.194
Sometimes I wonder, should I read the text first and then do all the bla bla bla afterwards?

150
01:20:02.194 --> 01:20:05.194
Or should I explain everything first and then read the text?

151
01:20:05.194 --> 01:20:08.194
But it doesn’t really matter much.

152
01:20:08.194 --> 01:20:09.194
We’re just going to do it.

153
01:20:09.194 --> 01:20:11.194
1 Chronicles chapter 21.

154
01:20:11.194 --> 01:20:19.194
At one point, the devil thought of bringing trouble to Israel.

155
01:20:19.194 --> 01:20:21.194
I find that so cool.

156
01:20:22.194 --> 01:20:27.194
Yes, because in Samuel it says that God did this.

157
01:20:27.194 --> 01:20:30.194
But you can’t handle that just yet.

158
01:20:30.194 --> 01:20:32.194
So we won’t talk about that today.

159
01:20:32.194 --> 01:20:38.194
If you want to know more about it, just talk to me one Monday evening after the prayer.

160
01:20:38.194 --> 01:20:39.194
And then we will talk about it.

161
01:20:39.194 --> 01:20:41.194
But then you go to bed with a problem.

162
01:20:41.194 --> 01:20:43.194
Because that is really, I love that theology.

163
01:20:43.194 --> 01:20:49.194
In Samuel it says that God advised David something.

164
01:20:49.194 --> 01:20:52.194
And here it says that the devil does that.

165
01:20:52.194 --> 01:20:55.194
Does the Bible contradict itself there?

166
01:20:55.194 --> 01:20:56.194
No.

167
01:20:56.194 --> 01:20:58.194
And we will leave it at that.

168
01:20:58.194 --> 01:21:00.194
I love that stuff. Delightful.

169
01:21:00.194 --> 01:21:04.194
At one point, the devil thought of something to bring Israel into trouble.

170
01:21:04.194 --> 01:21:09.194
He incited David to count the number of people in Israel.

171
01:21:09.194 --> 01:21:15.194
Then David said to Joab and the other commanders, go count how many men there are in all of Israel.

172
01:21:15.194 --> 01:21:17.194
Go through the whole country.

173
01:21:17.194 --> 01:21:23.194
From Dan in the north to Beersheba in the south and count the men of the people.

174
01:21:23.194 --> 01:21:26.194
I want to know how many men I can summon for the army.

175
01:21:26.194 --> 01:21:33.194
Joab said to the king, I hope that your Lord God will make the people a hundred times as many as they are now.

176
01:21:33.194 --> 01:21:37.194
The whole people serves you, my Lord the King.

177
01:21:37.194 --> 01:21:40.194
Why do you want to count the people?

178
01:21:40.194 --> 01:21:42.194
The Lord will punish Israel for that.

179
01:21:42.194 --> 01:21:47.194
But even though Joab and the commanders did not want to, the king insisted.

180
01:21:47.194 --> 01:21:53.194
So Joab and the commanders went through the whole country and returned to Jerusalem.

181
01:21:53.194 --> 01:21:56.194
Joab brought the king the outcome of the census.

182
01:21:56.194 --> 01:22:06.194
Israel had 1.1 million men who could go with the army.

183
01:22:06.194 --> 01:22:14.194
But the tribes of Levi and Benjamin had skipped Joab in the counting.

184
01:22:14.194 --> 01:22:18.194
For he found it terrible that the king wanted to count.

185
01:22:18.194 --> 01:22:24.194
God found it very wrong that David had done this.

186
01:22:24.194 --> 01:22:26.194
Therefore, He punished Israel.

187
01:22:26.194 --> 01:22:30.194
Then David said to God, this was very wrong for me.

188
01:22:30.194 --> 01:22:32.194
Lord, please forgive me.

189
01:22:33.194 --> 01:22:36.194
For what I have done is very foolish.

190
01:22:36.194 --> 01:22:42.194
Then the Lord said to David's prophet Gad, go to David and say to him,

191
01:22:42.194 --> 01:22:45.194
this says the Lord, choose how I will punish you.

192
01:22:45.194 --> 01:22:47.194
You can choose from three things.

193
01:22:47.194 --> 01:22:51.194
God went to David and said to him, this is what the Lord said, choose.

194
01:22:51.194 --> 01:22:57.194
Would you like three years of famine or three months of fleeing from your enemies who want to kill you?

195
01:22:57.194 --> 01:23:03.194
Or three days of plague in the land during which the angel of the Lord will bring death throughout the land?

196
01:23:03.194 --> 01:23:08.194
Think and consider what I should answer to Him who sent me.

197
01:23:08.194 --> 01:23:13.194
David answered, this is all equally terrible, but because God is good,

198
01:23:13.194 --> 01:23:18.194
it is better to fall into the hands of God than into the hands of men.

199
01:23:18.194 --> 01:23:21.194
So the Lord unleashed the plague on the land.

200
01:23:21.194 --> 01:23:24.194
70,000 people died.

201
01:23:24.194 --> 01:23:29.194
God sent the angel to Jerusalem to punish Jerusalem with the plague.

202
01:23:29.194 --> 01:23:32.194
But when the angel began, the Lord changed His mind.

203
01:23:32.194 --> 01:23:35.194
He said to the angel, that is enough, stop now.

204
01:23:35.194 --> 01:23:39.194
As if God had a pet child and that is Jerusalem.

205
01:23:39.194 --> 01:23:41.194
But that is for later.

206
01:23:41.194 --> 01:23:47.194
At that moment, the angel stood by the threshing floor of the Jebusite Ornan.

207
01:23:47.194 --> 01:23:51.194
David saw the angel of the Lord standing between heaven and earth.

208
01:23:51.194 --> 01:23:53.194
Wow, isn't that cool or what?

209
01:23:53.194 --> 01:24:00.194
David saw the angel of the Lord standing between heaven and earth with a drawn sword in his hand.

210
01:24:00.194 --> 01:24:03.194
He held that sword stretched out over Jerusalem.

211
01:24:03.194 --> 01:24:07.194
David and the leaders, dressed in mourning clothes, fell to the ground.

212
01:24:07.194 --> 01:24:12.194
And David cried out to God, it was my command to count the people.

213
01:24:12.194 --> 01:24:16.194
I have sinned against these poor sheep.

214
01:24:16.194 --> 01:24:17.194
What have they done?

215
01:24:17.194 --> 01:24:21.194
Please punish only me and my family.

216
01:24:21.194 --> 01:24:25.194
But leave your people alone and do not punish them.

217
01:24:25.194 --> 01:24:29.194
Then the angel of the Lord sent the prophet Gad to David.

218
01:24:29.194 --> 01:24:36.194
Gad had to say to David, build an altar for the Lord on the threshing floor of Ornan.

219
01:24:36.194 --> 01:24:37.194
Hallelujah.

220
01:24:37.194 --> 01:24:41.194
David obeyed Gad and did what the Lord had commanded.

221
01:24:41.194 --> 01:24:46.194
Ornan was at that moment threshing the wheat grains from the stalks.

222
01:24:46.194 --> 01:24:48.194
When he turned around, he saw the angel.

223
01:24:48.194 --> 01:24:51.194
His four sons were with him and they hid themselves.

224
01:24:51.194 --> 01:24:54.194
You see this phenomenon every time in the Bible.

225
01:24:54.194 --> 01:24:58.194
Whenever an angel appears, people become afraid.

226
01:24:58.194 --> 01:25:02.194
And that is because God is glorious.

227
01:25:02.194 --> 01:25:05.194
And He is just and He is amazing.

228
01:25:05.194 --> 01:25:06.194
So you should not think, oh that's an angel.

229
01:25:06.194 --> 01:25:07.194
Ah fun, an angel.

230
01:25:07.194 --> 01:25:08.194
No, wow.

231
01:25:08.194 --> 01:25:10.194
And then you get this effect.

232
01:25:10.194 --> 01:25:16.194
When Ornan saw David coming, he ran to him and bowed deeply before him.

233
01:25:16.194 --> 01:25:19.194
David said to him, I want to buy your threshing floor.

234
01:25:19.194 --> 01:25:21.194
Let me pay the full price.

235
01:25:21.194 --> 01:25:25.194
If you are taking notes, underline that.

236
01:25:25.194 --> 01:25:28.194
Let me pay the full price.

237
01:25:28.194 --> 01:25:30.194
I want to build an altar here for the Lord.

238
01:25:30.194 --> 01:25:32.194
Then the plague will stop.

239
01:25:32.194 --> 01:25:35.194
But Ornan answered, my Lord the King.

240
01:25:35.194 --> 01:25:38.194
Take what you want and do what you wish.

241
01:25:38.194 --> 01:25:41.194
Look, there are oxen for the offerings.

242
01:25:41.194 --> 01:25:46.194
The thirsty ones you may use as firewood and the grain as a meal offering.

243
01:25:46.194 --> 01:25:48.194
I give you everything.

244
01:25:48.194 --> 01:25:50.194
But King David said, no.

245
01:25:50.194 --> 01:25:54.194
I want to buy everything from you at full price.

246
01:25:54.194 --> 01:25:59.194
For I do not want to give anything that belongs to you to the Lord.

247
01:25:59.194 --> 01:26:04.194
I do not want to bring offerings to my God that cost me nothing.

248
01:26:04.194 --> 01:26:09.194
If you want to make notes in your Bible, underline that with a nice line.

249
01:26:09.194 --> 01:26:14.194
I do not want to bring offerings to my God that cost me nothing.

250
01:26:14.194 --> 01:26:19.194
Then David bought everything from Ornan for 600 shekels.

251
01:26:19.194 --> 01:26:21.194
That is 6.6 kilograms of gold.

252
01:26:21.194 --> 01:26:23.194
A nice amount these days.

253
01:26:23.194 --> 01:26:27.194
He built an altar there for the Lord and offered burnt offerings and thank offerings.

254
01:26:27.194 --> 01:26:29.194
He prayed to the Lord.

255
01:26:29.194 --> 01:26:35.194
The Lord answered him with fire from heaven on the burnt offering altar.

256
01:26:35.194 --> 01:26:41.194
Then the Lord commanded the angel to sheathe his sword.

257
01:26:41.194 --> 01:26:43.194
Shall we all say amen?

258
01:26:46.194 --> 01:26:50.194
Pride is what is being mentioned here.

259
01:26:50.194 --> 01:26:57.194
While we had concluded that Chronicles was a book of hope.

260
01:26:57.194 --> 01:27:03.194
How then do we encounter a story of sin now?

261
01:27:03.194 --> 01:27:07.194
I thought that Chronicles was just a book to say...

262
01:27:07.194 --> 01:27:12.194
Yes, we are going to do well. Yes, this is our faith. Yes, this is how we will handle it.

263
01:27:12.194 --> 01:27:17.194
This is our God of hope and everything will be alright and so we will rebuild.

264
01:27:17.194 --> 01:27:19.194
Do you know what I find so great?

265
01:27:19.194 --> 01:27:24.194
That precisely in such a book, like Chronicles, such a book of hope...

266
01:27:24.194 --> 01:27:28.194
that it also weaves in what we do wrong...

267
01:27:28.194 --> 01:27:31.194
but also how it can be made right again.

268
01:27:31.194 --> 01:27:33.194
That is where the hope lies.

269
01:27:33.194 --> 01:27:38.194
I am so glad with the people of Israel that we have a faith...

270
01:27:38.194 --> 01:27:42.194
in which the sin of humanity is also described...

271
01:27:42.194 --> 01:27:45.194
on the pages of the Scripture that we have.

272
01:27:45.194 --> 01:27:50.194
Imagine if the whole Bible were only a book of hope...

273
01:27:50.194 --> 01:27:54.194
in which only the proud achievements of humanity would be recorded.

274
01:27:54.194 --> 01:27:58.194
And this we have won and that we have won and this is how we have done well.

275
01:27:58.194 --> 01:28:02.194
Then we would have learned nothing, because we are all fallen people.

276
01:28:02.194 --> 01:28:05.194
We are all people who make mistakes.

277
01:28:05.194 --> 01:28:09.194
And how nice it is to learn from the pages of the Bible...

278
01:28:09.194 --> 01:28:13.194
where the Jews used to take the effort to write down...

279
01:28:13.194 --> 01:28:16.194
and here it went wrong and there it went wrong.

280
01:28:16.194 --> 01:28:19.194
And there David became proud.

281
01:28:19.194 --> 01:28:21.194
For here is the point, people.

282
01:28:21.194 --> 01:28:26.194
When I look at my own life, I see in many areas of my life...

283
01:28:26.194 --> 01:28:29.194
that I have been proud and often still am.

284
01:28:29.194 --> 01:28:35.194
And it is a struggle between myself and myself not to be proud.

285
01:28:35.194 --> 01:28:40.194
The question is whether you can also hold a mirror up to yourself today...

286
01:28:40.194 --> 01:28:43.194
and that you can reflect on yourself.

287
01:28:43.194 --> 01:28:47.194
And if you go home this week and take your personal prayers with you...

288
01:28:47.194 --> 01:28:51.194
about what pride is in our own lives.

289
01:28:51.194 --> 01:28:56.194
Because yes, to take stock in your own life about the number of troops...

290
01:28:56.194 --> 01:28:58.194
that you have, is David's story.

291
01:28:58.194 --> 01:29:02.194
But what is my story? What is your story?

292
01:29:02.194 --> 01:29:05.194
The Bible often comes...

293
01:29:05.194 --> 01:29:10.194
The Bible is continuously talking about pride and about arrogance.

294
01:29:10.194 --> 01:29:12.194
I want to say two things.

295
01:29:12.194 --> 01:29:15.194
First, I want to say that the Dutch word for pride...

296
01:29:15.194 --> 01:29:23.194
has a bit of a connotation that in pride is a form of sin.

297
01:29:23.194 --> 01:29:26.194
But I want to say first to the church...

298
01:29:26.194 --> 01:29:31.194
we as a church should not become hypocritical...

299
01:29:31.194 --> 01:29:37.194
by not wanting to be proud in a wrong way.

300
01:29:37.194 --> 01:29:39.194
Let me say it.

301
01:29:39.194 --> 01:29:42.194
I am proud of my children...

302
01:29:42.194 --> 01:29:46.194
when they come home with a good report card.

303
01:29:46.194 --> 01:29:51.194
And then it is good that I give my children a kiss and a hug...

304
01:29:51.194 --> 01:29:54.194
and that I say I am proud of you.

305
01:29:54.194 --> 01:29:56.194
So the Dutch word for being proud...

306
01:29:56.194 --> 01:30:01.194
is not necessarily the sin we are talking about here.

307
01:30:01.194 --> 01:30:04.194
Of course in the translation from the Hebrew...

308
01:30:04.194 --> 01:30:07.194
and from the Greek and the Latin...

309
01:30:07.194 --> 01:30:09.194
all those translations of the Bible...

310
01:30:09.194 --> 01:30:12.194
ultimately end up in our Dutch language.

311
01:30:12.194 --> 01:30:14.194
By the way, the beauty of the HSV...

312
01:30:14.194 --> 01:30:17.194
is that it is translated directly from the original language.

313
01:30:17.194 --> 01:30:19.194
So that is the cool thing about it.

314
01:30:19.194 --> 01:30:23.194
The HSV translation is not from the Hebrew...

315
01:30:23.194 --> 01:30:25.194
or the Aramaic of the Hebrew...

316
01:30:25.194 --> 01:30:28.194
then to the Greek or then to the Latin...

317
01:30:28.194 --> 01:30:30.194
and then finally arriving in our language.

318
01:30:30.194 --> 01:30:34.194
But the HSV Bible translators go straight to the origin.

319
01:30:34.194 --> 01:30:36.194
That is of course the most pure.

320
01:30:36.194 --> 01:30:38.194
The basic Bible that we have here...

321
01:30:38.194 --> 01:30:40.194
is an interpretative translation...

322
01:30:40.194 --> 01:30:42.194
and therefore there are still sometimes...

323
01:30:42.194 --> 01:30:45.194
some word discussions here and there.

324
01:30:45.194 --> 01:30:47.194
But I find it good enough...

325
01:30:47.194 --> 01:30:49.194
for simple people like me...

326
01:30:49.194 --> 01:30:51.194
that we use the basic Bible...

327
01:30:51.194 --> 01:30:54.194
and if we ever come to a nuance...

328
01:30:54.194 --> 01:30:57.194
I have a Bible verse from another translation...

329
01:30:57.194 --> 01:30:59.194
then we will tackle that nuance together.

330
01:30:59.194 --> 01:31:01.194
But the word pride, dear people...

331
01:31:01.194 --> 01:31:03.194
is not necessarily arrogance.

332
01:31:03.194 --> 01:31:06.194
So let me today address the word arrogance...

333
01:31:06.194 --> 01:31:09.194
as that one sinful way of pride.

334
01:31:09.194 --> 01:31:11.194
Is that a good idea?

335
01:31:11.194 --> 01:31:14.194
We don't have to flip through the pages with me...

336
01:31:14.194 --> 01:31:17.194
because I have a few Bible verses here...

337
01:31:17.194 --> 01:31:19.194
that I will read out loud shortly.

338
01:31:19.194 --> 01:31:22.194
But what David essentially does wrong...

339
01:31:22.194 --> 01:31:26.194
and this is where arrogance begins first...

340
01:31:26.194 --> 01:31:30.194
is that arrogance trusts in itself...

341
01:31:30.194 --> 01:31:32.194
instead of trusting in God.

342
01:31:32.194 --> 01:31:36.194
So actually the definition of pride for us Christians...

343
01:31:36.194 --> 01:31:40.194
is that we do not place our trust in the Lord.

344
01:31:40.194 --> 01:31:44.194
So if you actually go back to the principle of pride...

345
01:31:44.194 --> 01:31:47.194
that is actually where it all went wrong in the beginning.

346
01:31:47.194 --> 01:31:50.194
In the beginning, namely, God said to man...

347
01:31:50.194 --> 01:31:53.194
stay away from the tree.

348
01:31:53.194 --> 01:31:55.194
And man says...

349
01:31:55.194 --> 01:31:58.194
I think I can determine that for myself.

350
01:31:58.194 --> 01:32:01.194
In other words, instead of man...

351
01:32:01.194 --> 01:32:04.194
trusting in the command of God...

352
01:32:04.194 --> 01:32:07.194
and trusting in the provision of God...

353
01:32:07.194 --> 01:32:09.194
and God who says, mind you...

354
01:32:09.194 --> 01:32:11.194
I have given you everything.

355
01:32:11.194 --> 01:32:16.194
You may keep 99.9999%.

356
01:32:16.194 --> 01:32:19.194
They had the Garden of Eden, they had everything.

357
01:32:19.194 --> 01:32:22.194
They had trees and they had fruits.

358
01:32:22.194 --> 01:32:25.194
They had unity with the animals, they had unity with God.

359
01:32:25.194 --> 01:32:28.194
Adam had Eve, the most beautiful woman on earth...

360
01:32:28.194 --> 01:32:31.194
after Van Essendam.

361
01:32:31.194 --> 01:32:35.194
They had everything. Literally everything they had.

362
01:32:35.194 --> 01:32:38.194
And God says, you may enjoy everything.

363
01:32:38.194 --> 01:32:41.194
But there, one little point...

364
01:32:41.194 --> 01:32:43.194
you must stay away from that.

365
01:32:43.194 --> 01:32:46.194
And man, that is what I would like.

366
01:32:48.194 --> 01:32:52.194
And pride, instead of saying...

367
01:32:52.194 --> 01:32:55.194
when the Lord says it, obedience...

368
01:32:55.194 --> 01:33:00.194
pride says, I can certainly determine that myself?

369
01:33:00.194 --> 01:33:03.194
Pride says, I want to know.

370
01:33:03.194 --> 01:33:08.194
For I want to know how I can be joyful about something.

371
01:33:08.194 --> 01:33:13.194
I want to determine for myself how I can be happy about something.

372
01:33:13.194 --> 01:33:17.194
I want to determine for myself what can make me rich.

373
01:33:17.194 --> 01:33:20.194
I want to determine for myself how I can become wise.

374
01:33:20.194 --> 01:33:24.194
I want to determine for myself how I think I can approach God the Father.

375
01:33:24.194 --> 01:33:29.194
I want to determine for myself, because I think I am more important than God.

376
01:33:34.194 --> 01:33:38.194
Pride is actually disregarding God.

377
01:33:38.194 --> 01:33:43.194
Pride is placing yourself in a position where you are more important than God.

378
01:33:43.194 --> 01:33:48.194
Pride is the position where God actually does not matter.

379
01:33:48.194 --> 01:33:51.194
Therefore, I must, when I look around me...

380
01:33:51.194 --> 01:33:55.194
and I do not want to speak too fatalistically about the society we live in...

381
01:33:55.194 --> 01:33:58.194
but I find, when I look around me...

382
01:33:58.194 --> 01:34:04.194
that we live in an extremely proud society.

383
01:34:04.194 --> 01:34:11.194
That there is even a group in this world that calls itself pride.

384
01:34:11.194 --> 01:34:17.194
That there is even a group that speaks about the word pride, which means pride...

385
01:34:17.194 --> 01:34:22.194
but believe me, this is not pride in the way that I am proud of my children...

386
01:34:22.194 --> 01:34:24.194
who come home with a good report.

387
01:34:24.194 --> 01:34:29.194
The pride movement in this world openly says to itself...

388
01:34:29.194 --> 01:34:34.194
waving a flag, which is actually the promise of God...

389
01:34:34.194 --> 01:34:41.194
a whole group says, we are proud of how we want to behave...

390
01:34:41.194 --> 01:34:44.194
in the way we want to behave...

391
01:34:44.194 --> 01:34:50.194
and no one, absolutely no one, can tell us how we want to behave.

392
01:34:50.194 --> 01:34:58.194
And this movement is therefore happy to not be submissive to the Creator of heaven and earth.

393
01:34:58.194 --> 01:35:05.194
But even when I look around me and I just see how people in this society...

394
01:35:05.194 --> 01:35:08.194
are so self-centered...

395
01:35:08.194 --> 01:35:12.194
that you are so incredibly oriented...

396
01:35:12.194 --> 01:35:15.194
that you make yourself God.

397
01:35:15.194 --> 01:35:21.194
That you position yourself over your feelings, over your wisdom...

398
01:35:21.194 --> 01:35:24.194
over what you think, over your identity.

399
01:35:24.194 --> 01:35:26.194
It is all I.

400
01:35:26.194 --> 01:35:29.194
It is enormous, here comes the word egocentric.

401
01:35:29.194 --> 01:35:33.194
Ego means I, so it is enormously about the I.

402
01:35:33.194 --> 01:35:38.194
And this comes, and the Bible says this as well, several times...

403
01:35:38.194 --> 01:35:43.194
If you erase God, who do you have left as God?

404
01:35:43.194 --> 01:35:45.194
I.

405
01:35:45.194 --> 01:35:49.194
So when, for example, Romans chapter 1, brilliant chapter...

406
01:35:49.194 --> 01:35:52.194
read it at home in your personal study.

407
01:35:52.194 --> 01:35:57.194
But in Romans chapter 1 it says that the creator of heaven and earth...

408
01:35:57.194 --> 01:36:00.194
has made everything so beautifully.

409
01:36:00.194 --> 01:36:03.194
And he is so pleased with everything he has made.

410
01:36:03.194 --> 01:36:08.194
And the only thing he asks of his creation is that we recognize him as creator.

411
01:36:08.194 --> 01:36:12.194
But what people do is they no longer recognize the creator...

412
01:36:12.194 --> 01:36:14.194
and they push the creator away.

413
01:36:14.194 --> 01:36:16.194
What do you have left then?

414
01:36:16.194 --> 01:36:20.194
Then you have yourself left as the position of the universe.

415
01:36:20.194 --> 01:36:26.194
And then God says, if you do that, I can do nothing else...

416
01:36:26.194 --> 01:36:31.194
but to hand you over to your own evil desires.

417
01:36:32.194 --> 01:36:36.194
For what we just read contains something...

418
01:36:36.194 --> 01:36:39.194
that I often explain to the church.

419
01:36:39.194 --> 01:36:46.194
You see here in this powerful story that God punishes the people.

420
01:36:46.194 --> 01:36:49.194
And we talked about this some time ago...

421
01:36:49.194 --> 01:36:54.194
when I asked the church the question, does God punish?

422
01:36:54.194 --> 01:36:59.194
And what I want to present to the church is...

423
01:36:59.194 --> 01:37:03.194
it doesn't really matter much to me...

424
01:37:03.194 --> 01:37:08.194
about how you see God's punishment or the consequence of sin.

425
01:37:08.194 --> 01:37:11.194
Because to me, they are both the same.

426
01:37:11.194 --> 01:37:16.194
So, if you eat unhealthily, you get sick.

427
01:37:16.194 --> 01:37:21.194
So if you eat unhealthily, for example, if you use drugs, I would say...

428
01:37:21.194 --> 01:37:24.194
your body gets sick from that.

429
01:37:24.194 --> 01:37:32.194
Is then getting sick from the drugs, is that the punishment of God?

430
01:37:32.194 --> 01:37:37.194
Or is that the consequence of your unhealthy eating and drug use?

431
01:37:37.194 --> 01:37:41.194
So in our society, we prefer to stand together on the side of...

432
01:37:41.194 --> 01:37:45.194
that is simply a consequence of unhealthy eating.

433
01:37:45.194 --> 01:37:49.194
The Bible always takes the position, it is the punishment of God.

434
01:37:49.194 --> 01:37:51.194
Always.

435
01:37:51.194 --> 01:37:55.194
And I take the position of the Bible.

436
01:37:55.194 --> 01:37:58.194
In other words, God made us in such a way...

437
01:37:58.194 --> 01:38:01.194
that if we live for God, you are blessed.

438
01:38:01.194 --> 01:38:07.194
If you do not live for God, there is established by God in his truth...

439
01:38:07.194 --> 01:38:09.194
the consequence of sin.

440
01:38:09.194 --> 01:38:12.194
And that is what God has made.

441
01:38:12.194 --> 01:38:17.194
If God has set it up so that if you eat too much, you gain weight...

442
01:38:17.194 --> 01:38:19.194
then God has set it up that way.

443
01:38:19.194 --> 01:38:22.194
He is not sitting all the time perhaps behind the joystick to make me fatter...

444
01:38:22.194 --> 01:38:24.194
towards that tenth oliebol.

445
01:38:24.194 --> 01:38:25.194
Do you understand what I mean?

446
01:38:25.194 --> 01:38:30.194
He has made it so that there are consequences...

447
01:38:30.194 --> 01:38:32.194
of how we as humans live.

448
01:38:32.194 --> 01:38:36.194
Either in peace and obedience to God...

449
01:38:36.194 --> 01:38:42.194
or in the consequences of our sin, which the Bible calls punishment.

450
01:38:42.194 --> 01:38:46.194
And as we go through Chronicles chapter 21...

451
01:38:46.194 --> 01:38:50.194
and we see that the Angel of the Lord makes short work...

452
01:38:50.194 --> 01:38:54.194
with the sin of David, who is in pride...

453
01:38:54.194 --> 01:38:56.194
then I ask myself the question...

454
01:38:56.194 --> 01:38:59.194
how many of the things I have experienced in my life...

455
01:38:59.194 --> 01:39:04.194
where I have truly done myself a disservice.

456
01:39:04.194 --> 01:39:11.194
I have wasted years of my life doing foolish things.

457
01:39:11.194 --> 01:39:14.194
And because of that, I have had to bear consequences...

458
01:39:14.194 --> 01:39:16.194
that I would not wish on anyone.

459
01:39:16.194 --> 01:39:20.194
And so I see in the Bible that these are the punishments of God...

460
01:39:20.194 --> 01:39:25.194
from which I can ultimately be set free by the blood of Jesus.

461
01:39:25.194 --> 01:39:28.194
But that is why I must acknowledge that sin...

462
01:39:28.194 --> 01:39:32.194
and bring it to the cross of King Jesus.

463
01:39:32.194 --> 01:39:35.194
The Bible says in Proverbs, chapter 16 verse 18...

464
01:39:35.194 --> 01:39:38.194
you don't have to go along with me, because I will just go through it.

465
01:39:38.194 --> 01:39:41.194
The Bible is completely full of this.

466
01:39:41.194 --> 01:39:44.194
The Bible says in Proverbs 16 verse 18...

467
01:39:44.194 --> 01:39:48.194
if you become proud, it will end badly for you.

468
01:39:48.194 --> 01:39:51.194
If you are stubborn, you will fall.

469
01:39:51.194 --> 01:39:54.194
I actually want to give you this Bible verse.

470
01:39:54.194 --> 01:39:57.194
Especially in English, this is a saying.

471
01:39:57.194 --> 01:40:01.194
Pride comes for a fall.

472
01:40:01.194 --> 01:40:03.194
So if you want to take notes...

473
01:40:03.194 --> 01:40:07.194
these are life lessons that you can take into your personal life.

474
01:40:07.194 --> 01:40:10.194
Pride comes for a fall.

475
01:40:10.194 --> 01:40:13.194
In the English Christian world, this is a saying...

476
01:40:13.194 --> 01:40:17.194
this is a cliché based on this Bible verse.

477
01:40:17.194 --> 01:40:21.194
Pride always comes for a fall.

478
01:40:21.194 --> 01:40:25.194
When you are arrogant and you go through life...

479
01:40:25.194 --> 01:40:29.194
and you do not share in the sin of pride...

480
01:40:29.194 --> 01:40:35.194
then there is a 100% certainty that calamity will come into your life.

481
01:40:35.194 --> 01:40:39.194
The Creator has simply set it up this way.

482
01:40:39.194 --> 01:40:45.194
I can reflect on it a bit with you.

483
01:40:45.194 --> 01:40:49.194
Suppose there is someone in your circle of acquaintances...

484
01:40:49.194 --> 01:40:51.194
and they are always boasting about the Creator.

485
01:40:51.194 --> 01:40:55.194
They are always arrogant about how good they are.

486
01:40:55.194 --> 01:40:59.194
We humans actually have a bit of an urgh about that.

487
01:40:59.194 --> 01:41:03.194
And ultimately, you lose respect because of it...

488
01:41:03.194 --> 01:41:06.194
and even the friendship with that person.

489
01:41:06.194 --> 01:41:08.194
Do you understand what I mean?

490
01:41:08.194 --> 01:41:11.194
So from our human thinking, we actually see already...

491
01:41:11.194 --> 01:41:16.194
how disgusting pride really is in our lives.

492
01:41:16.194 --> 01:41:18.194
But God has said it this way.

493
01:41:18.194 --> 01:41:21.194
If you continue with pride...

494
01:41:21.194 --> 01:41:25.194
ultimately the Lord will deal with it.

495
01:41:25.194 --> 01:41:30.194
Pride recognizes itself and I want to show a few things about that.

496
01:41:30.194 --> 01:41:34.194
There are a few things that we as a church need to address...

497
01:41:34.194 --> 01:41:37.194
that we can prevent in our lives.

498
01:41:37.194 --> 01:41:41.194
One of the proud things we need to address as Christians...

499
01:41:41.194 --> 01:41:45.194
is the pride of thinking very highly of yourself.

500
01:41:45.194 --> 01:41:50.194
Jesus says in Luke chapter 18, verses 9 to 14...

501
01:41:50.194 --> 01:41:55.194
Jesus had noticed that some people considered themselves very religious...

502
01:41:55.194 --> 01:41:58.194
and looked down on other people.

503
01:41:58.194 --> 01:42:01.194
Therefore, he told them another story.

504
01:42:01.194 --> 01:42:04.194
He said two men went to the temple to pray.

505
01:42:04.194 --> 01:42:08.194
One was a Pharisee, the other was a tax collector.

506
01:42:08.194 --> 01:42:12.194
The Pharisee stood by himself and prayed...

507
01:42:12.194 --> 01:42:16.194
God, I thank you that I am not like all the other people.

508
01:42:16.194 --> 01:42:21.194
For they are greedy, dishonest, and unfaithful, but I am not.

509
01:42:21.194 --> 01:42:25.194
Thank you also that I am not like that tax collector over there.

510
01:42:25.194 --> 01:42:28.194
I fast twice a week...

511
01:42:28.194 --> 01:42:31.194
and I give you a tenth of all that I have.

512
01:42:31.194 --> 01:42:35.194
But the tax collector stood at a distance from the temple...

513
01:42:35.194 --> 01:42:38.194
and would not even look up to heaven.

514
01:42:38.194 --> 01:42:41.194
He beat his breast in sorrow and said...

515
01:42:41.194 --> 01:42:45.194
God, please forgive me for the bad things I have done.

516
01:42:45.194 --> 01:42:48.194
Have mercy on me, a sinner.

517
01:42:48.194 --> 01:42:53.194
I tell you, this tax collector went home justified before God...

518
01:42:53.194 --> 01:42:56.194
but the Pharisee did not.

519
01:42:56.194 --> 01:42:58.194
Here he comes.

520
01:42:58.194 --> 01:43:03.194
For everyone who exalts himself will be humbled.

521
01:43:03.194 --> 01:43:09.194
But if someone thinks very humbly of themselves, they will be saved.

522
01:43:11.194 --> 01:43:13.194
What did I say?

523
01:43:17.194 --> 01:43:20.194
That's just fine, isn't it?

524
01:43:21.194 --> 01:43:24.194
Do you think you are better than me?

525
01:43:26.194 --> 01:43:28.194
It's going okay, you know.

526
01:43:30.194 --> 01:43:35.194
But this is it. If someone thinks very humbly of themselves, they will be honored.

527
01:43:35.194 --> 01:43:37.194
And saved.

528
01:43:39.194 --> 01:43:43.194
Dear people, please. When you come to Open Church...

529
01:43:43.194 --> 01:43:49.194
you will certainly see the situations of many people around you.

530
01:43:49.194 --> 01:43:54.194
Please, look at the cross and do not look at people in Open Church.

531
01:43:54.194 --> 01:43:59.194
Dear people coming from other churches to this church, you are welcome in Open Church.

532
01:43:59.194 --> 01:44:04.194
I don't know what the reason is that you come to Open Church, but you are very welcome in Open Church.

533
01:44:04.194 --> 01:44:07.194
But I can guarantee you one thing in advance.

534
01:44:07.194 --> 01:44:12.194
If you come from another church to this church because you think things weren't good in that other church...

535
01:44:12.194 --> 01:44:16.194
and you are a few weeks in this church and you think things are good in this church...

536
01:44:16.194 --> 01:44:19.194
because Laura can play the piano beautifully...

537
01:44:19.194 --> 01:44:24.194
then you will soon find out that the reasons why you left your previous church...

538
01:44:24.194 --> 01:44:27.194
those reasons are also present here.

539
01:44:28.194 --> 01:44:31.194
I have seen people let go of their faith in Jesus Christ...

540
01:44:31.194 --> 01:44:35.194
and eventually I ran into them in the city and said to them, where are you then?

541
01:44:35.194 --> 01:44:39.194
And they say, I can no longer come to church because I see all those people with their hands in the air...

542
01:44:39.194 --> 01:44:43.194
and I know what he does wrong and I know what he does wrong and I know what he does wrong...

543
01:44:43.194 --> 01:44:47.194
and I will not go to a church where people have their hands in the air...

544
01:44:47.194 --> 01:44:49.194
of whom I know that they are bad people.

545
01:44:49.194 --> 01:44:54.194
I do not hear this just once in my life, I hear this dozens of times in my life.

546
01:44:54.194 --> 01:44:58.194
And every time the same answer is what I give back...

547
01:44:58.194 --> 01:45:02.194
praise God that people who make mistakes stand in church with their hands in the air.

548
01:45:03.194 --> 01:45:05.194
Praise God that those people still do that.

549
01:45:06.194 --> 01:45:12.194
Praise God that God goes through my heart and that no one else has to go through my heart.

550
01:45:12.194 --> 01:45:15.194
You would not be able to handle the mess in my heart...

551
01:45:15.194 --> 01:45:19.194
you would probably not be able to come back to this church because you would accuse me.

552
01:45:19.194 --> 01:45:22.194
But he who bled on a cross for me knows my heart...

553
01:45:22.194 --> 01:45:25.194
and he is the only one who may search my heart.

554
01:45:26.194 --> 01:45:31.194
What I want to convey with this is what the Bible says and Jesus teaches about this...

555
01:45:31.194 --> 01:45:35.194
please do not position yourself as a judge.

556
01:45:36.194 --> 01:45:40.194
For he says Jesus, he who judges another...

557
01:45:40.194 --> 01:45:44.194
by that same measure judgment will be given to you.

558
01:45:44.194 --> 01:45:46.194
If you condemn someone in the church...

559
01:45:46.194 --> 01:45:50.194
the one who may condemn you also comes, his name is Satan...

560
01:45:50.194 --> 01:45:52.194
and he will only come back to get you.

561
01:45:53.194 --> 01:45:57.194
And there is always something with this legalist that he can catch you on.

562
01:45:57.194 --> 01:46:00.194
For no one in this room is perfect.

563
01:46:01.194 --> 01:46:04.194
And that is why it is so important that we as Christians...

564
01:46:04.194 --> 01:46:08.194
position ourselves not as the Pharisee...

565
01:46:08.194 --> 01:46:10.194
but as the tax collector.

566
01:46:10.194 --> 01:46:12.194
Never position yourself.

567
01:46:12.194 --> 01:46:16.194
Even if you come here and I look at you across the room...

568
01:46:16.194 --> 01:46:21.194
and I have respect for people who have been here since day 1 of this church Reopold.

569
01:46:21.194 --> 01:46:24.194
And those people have been involved and have helped in the church.

570
01:46:24.194 --> 01:46:27.194
And they have given money to this church and they have prayed along.

571
01:46:27.194 --> 01:46:29.194
And they have provided leadership.

572
01:46:29.194 --> 01:46:34.194
But did you know that there is absolutely nothing you can appeal to...

573
01:46:34.194 --> 01:46:37.194
by saying, 'Where have I done that well?'

574
01:46:38.194 --> 01:46:42.194
There is absolutely nothing of which you can say, 'How much money I have given.'

575
01:46:43.194 --> 01:46:47.194
'How many years I have helped in this church.'

576
01:46:47.194 --> 01:46:50.194
'How great sermons I have given.'

577
01:46:50.194 --> 01:46:53.194
'How great a youth leader I am.'

578
01:46:53.194 --> 01:46:55.194
Absolutely nothing.

579
01:46:55.194 --> 01:47:00.194
As naked as Jesus hung on the cross for your sin.

580
01:47:00.194 --> 01:47:04.194
So naked you will ultimately stand before the Creator of heaven and earth.

581
01:47:04.194 --> 01:47:08.194
You have nothing to bring when it comes to your salvation.

582
01:47:08.194 --> 01:47:10.194
Nothing.

583
01:47:10.194 --> 01:47:13.194
We cannot appeal to anything.

584
01:47:13.194 --> 01:47:15.194
We are completely guilty.

585
01:47:15.194 --> 01:47:19.194
But through the blood of Jesus, we are completely saved.

586
01:47:19.194 --> 01:47:22.194
And clothed with the mantle of righteousness.

587
01:47:22.194 --> 01:47:24.194
He has put a ring on you.

588
01:47:24.194 --> 01:47:26.194
He has acquitted you of guilt.

589
01:47:26.194 --> 01:47:28.194
You are completely saved.

590
01:47:28.194 --> 01:47:30.194
Completely free.

591
01:47:30.194 --> 01:47:32.194
Shining white as snow.

592
01:47:32.194 --> 01:47:33.194
He loves you.

593
01:47:33.194 --> 01:47:37.194
But He loves you because of what He has done for you.

594
01:47:37.194 --> 01:47:39.194
Praise the Lord.

595
01:47:39.194 --> 01:47:40.194
I love him.

596
01:47:44.194 --> 01:47:48.194
In Matthew 6, verse 1, Jesus said to his disciples.

597
01:47:48.194 --> 01:47:51.194
Be good to other people.

598
01:47:51.194 --> 01:47:56.194
But do not do that to show everyone how great you are.

599
01:47:56.194 --> 01:48:00.194
For then you will not receive a reward from your heavenly Father.

600
01:48:01.194 --> 01:48:08.194
I want to take you through the reasoning I did for Open Church a few years ago.

601
01:48:08.194 --> 01:48:11.194
It was during Covid that we all hung up cameras.

602
01:48:11.194 --> 01:48:13.194
We were busy with YouTube.

603
01:48:13.194 --> 01:48:17.194
We were starting to get some YouTube subscribers.

604
01:48:18.194 --> 01:48:24.194
And I thought to myself ultimately about what I have seen go wrong in the world with the church.

605
01:48:24.194 --> 01:48:33.194
Eventually, I became sick of how the church often handles showcasing how great churches can be.

606
01:48:33.194 --> 01:48:36.194
Oh, in that church there are so many thousand people.

607
01:48:36.194 --> 01:48:39.194
Oh, in that church we had such a great service.

608
01:48:39.194 --> 01:48:45.194
Oh, in that church there were a thousand people getting baptized in one service with a lot of actors in the room.

609
01:48:45.194 --> 01:48:48.194
All just fuss. All just fuss.

610
01:48:48.194 --> 01:48:55.194
And eventually, Vanessa and I became so sick of it that we said we don't want this in our lives.

611
01:48:55.194 --> 01:49:00.194
We don't want the church to ultimately become a showroom for who Jesus is.

612
01:49:00.194 --> 01:49:04.194
You are a showroom when you live in love and relationship with God.

613
01:49:04.194 --> 01:49:06.194
Let your life shine.

614
01:49:06.194 --> 01:49:09.194
But the church and how we conduct our services.

615
01:49:09.194 --> 01:49:14.194
And we don't need to do close-ups when someone is praising the Lord with tears streaming down their face.

616
01:49:14.194 --> 01:49:16.194
Please, go away with that camera.

617
01:49:16.194 --> 01:49:20.194
Because no one has anything to do with it when someone is worshiping God.

618
01:49:20.194 --> 01:49:27.194
Maybe someone is magnifying God with a tear on their cheek because at that moment they feel like the tax collector.

619
01:49:27.194 --> 01:49:30.194
Have mercy on me, Lord. I'm a sinner.

620
01:49:30.194 --> 01:49:34.194
What does a camera have to do with that? Just go away with your camera, please.

621
01:49:34.194 --> 01:49:39.194
And ultimately it was the reasoning that I have positioned in the church.

622
01:49:39.194 --> 01:49:41.194
We are completely getting off social media.

623
01:49:41.194 --> 01:49:44.194
Because as far as I'm concerned, social media is clickbait.

624
01:49:44.194 --> 01:49:48.194
As far as I'm concerned, everyone can be on social media as much as they want.

625
01:49:48.194 --> 01:49:51.194
I have a Twitter account for real news.

626
01:49:53.194 --> 01:49:58.194
But look at me, click here. Look at me, click there. Look at me in the service, click.

627
01:49:58.194 --> 01:50:03.194
Look at me with the phone while I'm being baptized. Come on, man. Please.

628
01:50:04.194 --> 01:50:06.194
But it's all pride.

629
01:50:06.194 --> 01:50:09.194
It's all pride.

630
01:50:10.194 --> 01:50:18.194
That's why I see so many evangelical churches falling in these last five to ten years.

631
01:50:19.194 --> 01:50:23.194
Because what we are talking about here is that God is dealing with pride.

632
01:50:23.194 --> 01:50:29.194
And God is dealing with the churches in the world that are proud of how great they are.

633
01:50:32.194 --> 01:50:35.194
And in my prayer, people, please believe me.

634
01:50:35.194 --> 01:50:41.194
In my prayer, I have said to God, help us as a church to never fall into that trap.

635
01:50:41.194 --> 01:50:51.194
And if we do, if we do things wrong, help us here to be cleansed from the sin of pride.

636
01:50:51.194 --> 01:50:53.194
Because it is not worth it.

637
01:50:53.194 --> 01:50:57.194
You are not saved by a beautiful sermon, you are not saved by a nice new building.

638
01:50:57.194 --> 01:51:01.194
The new building we are going to build has nothing to do with your salvation.

639
01:51:01.194 --> 01:51:07.194
The new building we are going to build is not to show off how great a church we are.

640
01:51:07.194 --> 01:51:12.194
The new building we are going to build is so that we can explain what the Bible says about pride.

641
01:51:12.194 --> 01:51:18.194
So that people can come and come to repentance in the name of Jesus, the cross that we set down there.

642
01:51:18.194 --> 01:51:22.194
But please let us push pride out of our lives.

643
01:51:22.194 --> 01:51:26.194
Pride on a spiritual level, do not do that.

644
01:51:27.194 --> 01:51:31.194
Pride about how good you are and how much you have given.

645
01:51:31.194 --> 01:51:35.194
The Bible also says, what your right hand gives, you should not let your left hand know.

646
01:51:35.194 --> 01:51:39.194
In other words, if you are helping someone in your circle of acquaintances.

647
01:51:39.194 --> 01:51:42.194
Someone's car is broken, and you might want to help that person.

648
01:51:42.194 --> 01:51:46.194
And you say, you know what, I will pay for the repair costs of that car.

649
01:51:46.194 --> 01:51:48.194
You should not tell other people about it.

650
01:51:48.194 --> 01:51:50.194
Just keep that to yourself.

651
01:51:50.194 --> 01:51:55.194
Suppose the Holy Spirit tells you in your prayer, I want you to buy a bag of groceries for that person.

652
01:51:55.194 --> 01:51:58.194
Then do that, and be quiet about it.

653
01:51:58.194 --> 01:52:00.194
Let no one know about it.

654
01:52:00.194 --> 01:52:02.194
By all means, do such things.

655
01:52:04.194 --> 01:52:11.194
By all means, be led by the Holy Spirit to do good works.

656
01:52:11.194 --> 01:52:13.194
Just a mini side street.

657
01:52:13.194 --> 01:52:22.194
When was the last time you did a good work for a brother or sister in God's kingdom?

658
01:52:23.194 --> 01:52:25.194
Point.

659
01:52:26.194 --> 01:52:29.194
Right? Good self-reflection.

660
01:52:29.194 --> 01:52:31.194
For the Lord says that we must do that.

661
01:52:31.194 --> 01:52:33.194
And then don't brag about it.

662
01:52:33.194 --> 01:52:38.194
So this week everyone to Jumbo, buy bags of food for various people.

663
01:52:38.194 --> 01:52:40.194
You understand what I mean, right?

664
01:52:42.194 --> 01:52:44.194
Proverbs 13 verse 10, I'm almost closing.

665
01:52:44.194 --> 01:52:46.194
Proverbs 13 verse 10 says the following words.

666
01:52:46.194 --> 01:52:53.194
People who think they know everything cause strife, but those who listen to good advice are wise.

667
01:52:57.194 --> 01:52:58.194
I love the proverbs.

668
01:52:58.194 --> 01:53:01.194
Why? The proverbs are always those one-liners.

669
01:53:01.194 --> 01:53:04.194
And believe me, if you have just been converted.

670
01:53:04.194 --> 01:53:06.194
Dear people, listen carefully to what I say.

671
01:53:06.194 --> 01:53:12.194
If you have just been converted and you find the Bible quite difficult, just read proverbs for the coming year.

672
01:53:12.194 --> 01:53:17.194
Just do proverbs. Just do one chapter of proverbs a day.

673
01:53:17.194 --> 01:53:18.194
You will become very wise from that.

674
01:53:20.194 --> 01:53:21.194
Great book.

675
01:53:22.194 --> 01:53:28.194
I repeat, people who think they know everything cause strife, but those who listen to good advice are wise.

676
01:53:28.194 --> 01:53:40.194
To all the people in this room, who are intellectual, who have learned a lot, who are successful in their careers, who have a good job.

677
01:53:43.194 --> 01:53:49.194
Never position yourself as a be-all and end-all.

678
01:53:49.194 --> 01:54:00.194
Do not position yourself as if no one can teach me anything anymore, because that blocks your capacity to enter into worship.

679
01:54:01.194 --> 01:54:09.194
If you position yourself, the Bible, do I have that with me? No, I had so many Bible verses.

680
01:54:09.194 --> 01:54:18.194
In English it also says, knowledge puffs up, wisdom builds up.

681
01:54:19.194 --> 01:54:24.194
And so pride, one of the things we need to address in our church when it comes to pride,

682
01:54:24.194 --> 01:54:30.194
is that if you are a smart guy or a smart young lady, and you are very intellectual,

683
01:54:31.194 --> 01:54:36.194
always be humble enough to learn more from other people.

684
01:54:36.194 --> 01:54:42.194
Always position yourself in such a way that the person who is talking to you,

685
01:54:42.194 --> 01:54:46.194
might have something to say from which you can learn more.

686
01:54:47.194 --> 01:54:57.194
Here is another self-check. When was the last time you could say to someone, ah, that is a good point.

687
01:54:58.194 --> 01:55:02.194
Ah, I think you are right. Just think about it, think for a moment.

688
01:55:02.194 --> 01:55:16.194
Because here is the other side. If you reflect on yourself and think back to your marriage, your family, your church, your family circle,

689
01:55:16.194 --> 01:55:27.194
if you are always on the defense, if it is always the case that you are right and you have not said to anyone in the past year,

690
01:55:27.194 --> 01:55:34.194
that is a good point you are making. You are right. Then you are dealing with pride.

691
01:55:35.194 --> 01:55:45.194
One hundred percent. Then you need to deal with pride. Because by no means can there be anyone in this room who is always right, who knows everything.

692
01:55:46.194 --> 01:55:52.194
That simply cannot be. There is always something you do not know. Even if it is just the emotion of that other person.

693
01:55:53.194 --> 01:56:01.194
Suppose you can tell everything about what that person is doing wrong. And that person comes with their broken heart. Did you not know?

694
01:56:02.194 --> 01:56:08.194
So you should never say that you know everything. Because the one who knows everything ultimately has nothing more to say.

695
01:56:08.194 --> 01:56:17.194
And if they have nothing more to say, and if that, check this, if that becomes your heart's position, then your heart becomes hard.

696
01:56:17.194 --> 01:56:29.194
And if your heart becomes hard, and then you read the Bible, and the Bible shakes your knowledge tremendously, did you just read this story with me or not?

697
01:56:30.194 --> 01:56:39.194
And we just read this story, that the angel, that the prophet comes to David, and that the prophet says, you may choose from three punishments.

698
01:56:40.194 --> 01:56:52.194
What does that do to your mind? If you position yourself as mister or missus knowledge, I know everything, then you already have a problem here.

699
01:56:52.194 --> 01:56:58.194
Because the Bible is not always easy for your rational thinking. Right?

700
01:56:59.194 --> 01:57:13.194
So what you need to do is regularly do a self-check in the coming weeks, and have you positioned yourself in such a way that you regularly say to other people, good point.

701
01:57:13.194 --> 01:57:21.194
Ah yes, you are right about that. Or also, sorry, I was wrong. Very important.

702
01:57:21.194 --> 01:57:32.194
When was the last time you said sorry to someone else, when you were wrong, when you were unreasonable, when you were proud?

703
01:57:32.194 --> 01:57:40.194
For the antidote, the strongest antidote against pride, is saying sorry. Just try it once.

704
01:57:40.194 --> 01:57:48.194
If you can say sorry to someone, at that moment you have overcome pride. Because pride really does not say sorry.

705
01:57:51.194 --> 01:58:05.194
In Philippians 2, verses 1 to 11, I ultimately showed at the beginning of this service how Jesus Christ is the ultimate Lord,

706
01:58:05.194 --> 01:58:15.194
who could have remained in his pride and could have said, I am God. I am the Creator of heaven and earth.

707
01:58:15.194 --> 01:58:23.194
I have everything. I am already holy. I am already perfect. I am already entitled to all glory and honor.

708
01:58:23.194 --> 01:58:29.194
And Jesus showed at the cross what it is to put pride down.

709
01:58:29.194 --> 01:58:35.194
We have already read it together at the beginning of this service, and I will read it again together with you now.

710
01:58:35.194 --> 01:58:39.194
You don't have to read it out loud with me, but I will just take a look at it together.

711
01:58:39.194 --> 01:58:49.194
Can we look at those verses? This is the master of humility. Jesus is the master of being completely not proud.

712
01:58:49.194 --> 01:58:56.194
Jesus is the master who shows how you never have to fall for pride.

713
01:58:56.194 --> 01:59:03.194
